---

import Layout from "../Layout/Layout.astro";
import before from "../assets/Before.jpg";
import after from "../assets/After.jpg";
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
const citations = [
    {
        Inline: "Ignore me",
        mla: ""
    },
]
---


<Layout  title="Theological Mandate" Citations={citations}>
    <div class="u-container flex flex-col content-center">
        <div class="flex-auto h-full w-full pt-40 z-2 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-black py-5" data-sy-reveal="chars">
                Disruptive action
            </h1>
            <div class="content-center justify-center items-center flex flex-col">
                <p class="w-3/4 font-bold text-lg p-4" data-sy-reveal="words">
                    Our argument has been long and winding so far, and we should summarize.
                </p>
                <div class="grid grid-flow-row gap-4 items-center place-content-center py-4">
                    <div class="bg-red-300 rounded-lg border-2 py-4 px-6 items-center w-3/4 place-self-center">
                        <p class="pb-4">
                            Our main premise:
                        </p>
                        <div class="items-center">
                            <p class="text-left">

                                1. If the lack of healthcare access for trans people negatively affects those people, that lack of access is wrong.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-left">
                                2. The lack of healthcare access for trans people negatively affects trans people.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-left">
                                C. Therefore that lack of access is wrong.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="pt-4 w-7/8 place-self-center">
                        In other words, the lack of healthcare access for trans people actively hurts those people by requiring them to forgo important healthcare that
                        is needed to live a fulfilling life. In the American South,
                        there exists a bias and prejudice against transgender people that manifests in the form of a lack of healthcare resources for those transgender people,
                        caused by a number of factors like harmful legislation, reduction of resource providers,
                        and a dangerous political climate. This has lead to a significant negative impact on the mental and physical health of the transgender people affected,
                        seen through high rates of suicide and violence toward transgender people.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        In the ethical mandate, the framework we used required us to extend our circles of care,
                        which would require us to extend our care to trans people as well.
                        Since healthcare and the ability to live a good life is an important part of providing care, these need to also be expanded to trans people too.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Throughout our theological mandate, it was proved that trans people deserve the same dignity and well treatment as any other humans.
                        The prevention of the healthcare needed to live their lives fulfilling threatens the life and dignity of trans people.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        We need to keep Solidarity with these trans people to restore their dignity that is being violated.
                        It is important because there are physical needs to be met like food and shelter,
                        but also mental ones like being able to converse with others and have a connection with that.
                        For transgender people in the South, a lot of institutions and safety nets in place do not apply to the problems they face.
                        Furthermore, solidarity is needed in order to gather enough people to make change in communities so that trans people can
                        get the support and healthcare they deserve.
                    </p>
                    <div class="py-2"/>
                    <div  class="collapse collapse-arrow bg-white/25 bg-base-100 border-base-300 border">
                        <input type="checkbox" />
                        <div class="collapse-title font-semibold">Sofia Cano</div>
                        <div class="collapse-content text-sm w-3/4 place-self-center">
                            <p class="">
                                Sofia Cano is suffering because of the system under which she lives. Not just the prison,
                                but the state and country as well. This is not something easily helped with charity.
                                Though it is possible to help the efforts of organizations like the ACLU,
                                it’s more important to try and convince the people in charge. This can be done through activism, not just through money.
                            </p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex flex-col w-full items-center">
                        <h1 class="text-xl font-bold pt-4" data-sy-reveal="chars">
                            5 why analysis
                        </h1>
                        <span class="w-1/8 h-1 bg-black/50 rounded-2xl self-center" />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="py-8 flex">
                    <ul class="timeline timeline-snap-icon max-md:timeline-compact timeline-vertical">
                        <li>
                            <div class="timeline-middle">
                                <svg
                                        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                        viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                        fill="currentColor"
                                        class="h-5 w-5"
                                >
                                    <path
                                            fill-rule="evenodd"
                                            d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                            clip-rule="evenodd"
                                    />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end scroll-m-40 target:animate-cite rounded-l">
                                <time class="font-mono italic">Why #1</time>
                                <div class="text-lg font-black leading-none pb-2 flex flex-row items-center target:animate-cite" data-sy-reveal="lines">The system is not allowing Cano to complete her transition, and actively disrespects her identity because the prison is enacting new policies against trans people.</div>
                            </div>
                            <hr />
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <hr />
                            <div class="timeline-middle">
                                <svg
                                        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                        viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                        fill="currentColor"
                                        class="h-5 w-5"
                                >
                                    <path
                                            fill-rule="evenodd"
                                            d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                            clip-rule="evenodd"
                                    />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <div class="timeline-end md:mb-10 scroll-m-40 target:animate-cite rounded-l" >
                                <div class="w-fit self-start"><time class="font-mono italic text-left">Why #2</time></div>
                                <div class="text-lg text-left font-black leading-none pb-2 flex flex-row items-center target:animate-cite" data-sy-reveal="lines">This is because of a South Carolina house bill (4624) which was passed.</div>
                            </div>
                            <hr />
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class="timeline-middle">
                                <svg
                                        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                        viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                        fill="currentColor"
                                        class="h-5 w-5"
                                >
                                    <path
                                            fill-rule="evenodd"
                                            d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                            clip-rule="evenodd"
                                    />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end scroll-m-40 target:animate-cite rounded-l">
                                <time class="font-mono italic">Why #3</time>
                                <div class="text-lg font-black leading-none pb-2 flex flex-row items-center target:animate-cite" data-sy-reveal="lines">This law bans medically necessary healthcare for trans youth, and the use of public funds for trans patients.</div>
                            </div>
                            <hr />
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <hr />
                            <div class="timeline-middle">
                                <svg
                                        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                        viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                        fill="currentColor"
                                        class="h-5 w-5"
                                >
                                    <path
                                            fill-rule="evenodd"
                                            d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                            clip-rule="evenodd"
                                    />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <div class="timeline-end md:mb-10 scroll-m-40 target:animate-cite rounded-l" >
                                <div class="w-fit self-start"><time class="font-mono italic text-left">Why #4</time></div>
                                <div class="text-lg text-left font-black leading-none pb-2 flex flex-row items-center target:animate-cite" data-sy-reveal="lines">Lawmakers like Thomas Beach and Nancy Mace are behind this bill, because of their misinformed beliefs about trans people.</div>
                            </div>
                            <hr />
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <hr />
                            <div class="timeline-middle">
                                <svg
                                        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                        viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                        fill="currentColor"
                                        class="h-5 w-5"
                                >
                                    <path
                                            fill-rule="evenodd"
                                            d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                            clip-rule="evenodd"
                                    />
                                </svg>
                            </div>
                            <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end scroll-m-40 target:animate-cite rounded-l" id="source7">
                                <time class="font-mono italic">Why #5</time>
                                <div class="text-lg text-right font-black leading-none pb-2 flex flex-row items-center target:animate-cite" data-sy-reveal="lines">These beliefs are caused by a lack of information about the medical necessity of transition.</div>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="flex flex-col w-full items-center">
                        <h1 class="text-xl font-bold pt-4" data-sy-reveal="chars">
                            Design thinking
                        </h1>
                        <span class="w-1/8 h-1 bg-black/50 rounded-2xl self-center" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="py-4">
                        The design thinking process we used had us graphing a bunch of different ideas which our group had on a graph of ease of implementation vs impact.
                        Our question was how we might organize more public resources for healthcare providers and the general public to learn about trans people and their needs.
                    </p>
                    <div class="px-24 place-content-center self-center">
                        <figure class="diff aspect-3/4 rounded-2xl" tabindex="0">
                            <div class="diff-item-1" role="img" tabindex="0">
                                <div class="bg-primary text-primary-content grid place-content-center text-9xl font-black">
                                    <Image src={before} alt="before image" class="object-contain"/>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="diff-item-2" role="img">
                                <div class="bg-base-200 grid place-content-center text-9xl font-black">
                                    <Image src={after} alt="before image" class="object-contain"/>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="diff-resizer place-self-end"></div>
                        </figure>
                        <p class="text-sm">
                            The images above demonstrate the culling process.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="py-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
                        <div class="flex flex-col w-full items-center">
                            <h1 class="text-xl font-bold pt-4" data-sy-reveal="chars">
                                The Solution
                            </h1>
                            <span class="w-1/8 h-1 bg-black/50 rounded-2xl self-center" />
                        </div>
                        <p class="w-7/8 self-center">
                            Our solution that we prototyped was creating more required classes for doctors and healthcare providers that specifically
                            educated them on caring for trans patients. Many trans people struggle to find healthcare environments that can properly
                            care for them and that they can feel safe because people are unaware of how to treat them right. This is also why a big part
                            of the solution is having doctors work with transgender patients to develop these classes, and have their input on the issue.
                            Historically, a lot of decisions about legality of transition, treatment of patients, and insurance coverage are made without
                            any input from transgender people. This has led to a lot of the abuses that we see in the healthcare system like a lack of coverage
                            for life-saving gender-affirming care and a lot of arbitrary bureaucracy that trans people need to go through in order to get gender-affirming care.
                            Getting trans people involved with this solution excites us the most, as it not only helps address the healthcare issues they face but
                            also allows them to have a voice and an impact in a place where they have historically been ignored or abused.
                        </p>
                        <p class="w-7/8 self-center">
                            Success with this solution would look like trans people being able to receive the proper care and understanding
                            from healthcare advisors without feeling like those providers were uneducated on those issues.
                            It would mean that they would feel safe to be themselves and be treated as the gender they chose,
                            rather than having to clarify and keep advocating for themselves just for people to use the right pronouns.
                            It would mean that the healthcare system as a whole would work to support and facilitate their transition rather
                            than setting up more hurdles like inconsistent prescription access and direct denial of gender affirming care on
                            discretion of the healthcare providers that trans people go through in order to receive healthcare.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>